        <article class="lesson-article">
            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 4</span><h1>ValueTask for Performance</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>25 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Why ValueTask?</h2>
                    <p>Task is a reference type—every async call allocates. ValueTask is a struct that can avoid allocations when the result is available synchronously.</p>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>When to Use ValueTask</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Perfect for methods that often complete synchronously
public class Cache
{
    private readonly Dictionary&lt;string, Data&gt; _cache = new();

    // Often returns cached value (sync), sometimes fetches (async)
    public async ValueTask&lt;Data&gt; GetAsync(string key)
    {
        if (_cache.TryGetValue(key, out var cached))
            return cached;  // No allocation!

        var data = await FetchFromDatabaseAsync(key);
        _cache[key] = data;
        return data;
    }
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>ValueTask Rules</h2>
                    <div class="warning-box">
                        <div class="warning-box-header"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg><span>Important Rules</span></div>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Never await a ValueTask more than once</li>
                            <li>Never use .Result or .GetAwaiter().GetResult() before completion</li>
                            <li>If you need multiple awaits, convert to Task first</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// ❌ WRONG - awaiting twice
var valueTask = GetAsync(key);
var result1 = await valueTask;
var result2 = await valueTask;  // Undefined behavior!

// ✅ CORRECT - convert to Task if needed
var task = GetAsync(key).AsTask();
var result1 = await task;
var result2 = await task;  // Safe</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Task vs ValueTask</h2>
                    <div class="comparison-grid">
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>Use Task</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Public API surfaces</li>
                                <li>When caching the result</li>
                                <li>General-purpose async</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>Use ValueTask</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Hot paths with sync completion</li>
                                <li>Performance-critical code</li>
                                <li>IAsyncEnumerable</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
                    <div class="takeaways">
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>ValueTask avoids allocations for sync completion.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Only await ValueTask once!</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Use Task for public APIs, ValueTask for hot paths.</span></div>
                    </div>
                </section>
